#: ../../source/templates_uber.md
msgid "Keyboard focus indicators"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_uber.md:220
msgid ""
"**Shadow Philosophy**: Uber uses shadow purely as a structural tool, "
"never decoratively. Shadows are always black at very low opacity "
"(0.08-0.16), creating the bare minimum lift needed to separate content "
"layers. The blur radii are moderate (8-16px) -- enough to feel natural "
"but never dramatic. There are no colored shadows, no layered shadow "
"stacks, and no ambient glow effects. Depth is communicated more through "
"the black/white section contrast than through shadow elevation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_uber.md:222
msgid "7. Do's and Don'ts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_uber.md:224
msgid "Do"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_uber.md:225
msgid ""
"Use true black (`#000000`) and pure white (`#ffffff`) as the primary "
"palette -- the stark contrast IS Uber"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_uber.md:226
msgid ""
"Use 999px border-radius for all buttons, chips, and pill-shaped "
"navigation elements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_uber.md:227
msgid "Keep all headings in UberMove Bold (700) for billboard-level impact"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_uber.md:228
msgid ""
"Use whisper-soft shadows (0.12-0.16 opacity) for card elevation -- barely"
" visible"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_uber.md:229
msgid ""
"Maintain the compact, information-dense layout style -- Uber prioritizes "
"efficiency over airiness"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_uber.md:230
msgid "Use warm, human-centric illustrations to soften the monochrome interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_uber.md:231
msgid "Apply 8px radius for content cards and 12px for featured containers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_uber.md:232
msgid "Use UberMoveText at weight 500 for navigation and prominent UI text"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_uber.md:233
msgid ""
"Pair black primary buttons with white secondary buttons for dual-action "
"layouts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_uber.md:235
msgid "Don't"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_uber.md:236
msgid ""
"Don't introduce color into the UI chrome -- Uber's interface is strictly "
"black, white, and gray"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_uber.md:237
msgid ""
"Don't use rounded corners less than 999px on buttons -- the full-pill "
"shape is a core identity element"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_uber.md:238
msgid ""
"Don't apply heavy shadows or drop shadows with high opacity -- depth is "
"whisper-subtle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_uber.md:239
msgid ""
"Don't use serif fonts anywhere -- Uber's typography is exclusively "
"geometric sans-serif"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_uber.md:240
msgid ""
"Don't create airy, spacious layouts with excessive whitespace -- Uber's "
"density is intentional"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_uber.md:241
msgid ""
"Don't use gradients or color overlays -- every surface is a flat, solid "
"color"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_uber.md:242
msgid ""
"Don't mix UberMove into body text or UberMoveText into headlines -- the "
"hierarchy is strict"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_uber.md:243
msgid ""
"Don't use decorative borders -- borders are functional (inputs, dividers)"
" or absent entirely"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_uber.md:244
msgid ""
"Don't soften the black/white contrast with off-whites or near-blacks -- "
"the duality is deliberate"
msgstr ""

